            <sparkle:version>1503</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.15.3</h2>
<p><b>Joining a call is useful again.</b> Jarvis used to greet every call with
"Need a hand on this call?" — and the briefing behind it was a demo, showing
example people instead of the meeting you were actually in.</p>

<h3>When a call starts</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Joining a call now offers to start a transcript, the one thing Jarvis can
      really do on a call. The demo briefing no longer takes that prompt's
      place.</li>
  <li>The briefing is still there for showing the idea — it opens from the
      Jarvis menu's "Assist Me on This Call", or ⌘⇧A.</li>
  <li>Settings → Meetings still has the switch if you want the offer back, and
      now says plainly that the briefing shows example people. If you had
      already switched it on, it stays on.</li>
</ul>

<p>No change to what leaves your Mac: audio is captured on your machine, Slack
is searched live and never stored, and mail and meetings stay local.</p>
]]></description>
